Subject: [PATCH 08114/11362] [outer-loop] Verification pass on the
 goal-evidence A/B: hidden-game reach claim retracted, GROUNDED shown not to
 discriminate

Every finding was reproduced from the run's own files before anything was edited. Nothing in
out/preregistration.json, out/rows.json or out/analysis.json was touched, so
reproducibility_checksum and prereg_sha256 both still verify against the committed values.

works_on_an_unsolved_game was FALSE and is now false. Not one unsolved game was measured: all 20
roster games are full_game_clear in ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml, and every window came from
build_progress_window -> exp5717.build_window -> solve_adaptered(game, 1), which returns None
unless the game solves to L1 offline through a registered GameAdapter. split_meta records
levelup_rows_in_heldout: 1 for all 20, so "stall games with zero observed wins are in the roster
on purpose" is contradicted by the harness's own witness; the verified claim is the narrower
levelup_rows_in_shown == 0. The tn36 existence proof was worse -- full_game_clear, 7 levels
reproduced, four outer-loop source reads in its registry entry, and ZERO cells in this run -- and
is deleted. The unstated confound behind it is now recorded: prompt CONTENT is clean but
transition SELECTION is solve-conditioned, since the window is a banked winning route cut at the
L0->L1 boundary while a hidden game yields an exploration buffer. This is not a provenance
violation: development_proxy was declared correctly and adversarial_verify flags nothing.

GROUNDED is a syntax label, not an evidence label. Re-scoring every captured predicate against a
DIFFERENT game's transitions preserves the label on 262 of 285 comparisons; all four GROUNDED
cells survive under 17-19 of 19 foreign games, including the single cell that produced the
treatment arm's grounded_rate=1.0. The accepting set averages 65.9% of the literal space and
literal 0 alone grounds on 17 of 20 games. Two behaviour-preserving rewrites on real cells:
`return False` -> `return False and grid[0, 0] == 4` flips all five DECLINED cells to GROUNDED,
exactly inverting the reported S2-B/S2-C result; an alpha-rename or operand swap flips TROPE
cells. PRIMARY and TROPE re-checked and still clean.

Also: min_reachable_p 0.0 was the DESIGN's floor -- at the achieved n the smallest attainable p is
0.25, and 1.0 on the PRIMARY, so NON-TEST is structural. The split-vs-combined partition is a
one-directional proxy, making 3.4 points a lower bound on the knobs' reach rather than a ceiling.
An internal contradiction between known_confounds and its own byte-identity DIAGNOSIS is resolved
in favour of the DIAGNOSIS.

Found while applying the above: the artifact was not the output of its own builder --
exhibit_truncation and known_confounds lived in the committed file and in no code path, 47 leaf
differences on rebuild. Both are now constructed in build_artifact.py. artifact_freshness_lint did
not fire because this artifact is unregistered, the coverage limit its own docstring names.

The arc_executable_world_model.py docstring narrowing is docstring-only: both versions parsed with
every docstring stripped from the AST give identical ast.dump (bb71fe38bdc9dd71). That proof is
the evidence in each of the 7 freshness acknowledgements.

Defaults unchanged: both knobs still ship OFF. No scored or online ARC game was played;
submission is operator-only.

